{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp","id":1051059,"title":"Feeding at high BP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-18T10:40:25-08:00","id":1051059,"title":"Feeding at high BP","content":"In some big city, is not weird to have more than one vampire at BP 6 or higher. <br /> How can such vampires feed to sustain themself? How can they deal with the vinculum if they leave the &quot;food&quot; alive?<br /> <br /> I'd like to collect a list of suggestion and ideas about this particular subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T11:00:16-08:00","id":1051065,"title":"","content":"Options:<br /> Get some vampires that can't cause a Vinculum (it is the weakness of a few bloodlines)<br /> Develop the ability to feed from other supernaturals (if available)<br /> Deal with a Vinculum (maybe you bind them first with your own)<br /> Use Blood Sorcery or Oaths to get Vitae indirectly.<br /> Drink from lesser sources and burn Willpower to convert to Vitae","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T11:20:41-08:00","id":1051074,"title":"","content":"Get the Touch of Deprivation devotion, use it on yourself to temporarily nullify your sense of taste. Feed. <br /> <br /> Put yourself under vinculum to someone in torpor or lives far away or is nomadic. You can feed off whoever else you want.<br /> <br /> Use the Cruac rituals or Invictus oaths that let you leech off someone else's vitae consumption.<br /> <br /> Choose a cliche mask and dirge to farm willpower and continue to feed off humans as needed. <br /> <br /> Mix and match these combos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T11:39:16-08:00","id":1051077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051074#post1051074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get the Touch of Deprivation devotion, use it on yourself to temporarily nullify your sense of taste. Feed. <br /> <br /> Put yourself under vinculum to someone in torpor or lives far away or is nomadic. You can feed off whoever else you want.<br /> <br /> Use the Cruac rituals or Invictus oaths that let you leech off someone else's vitae consumption.<br /> <br /> Choose a cliche mask and dirge to farm willpower and continue to feed off humans as needed. <br /> <br /> Mix and match these combos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Vampire be vinculated to only one vampire at time? I didn't know this...<br /> <br /> Why should the sense of taste be the reason of a vinculum? Isn't it a mistical effect due to ingestion ov vampiric vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:17:17-08:00","id":1051088,"title":"","content":"Stage 3 Vinculum prevents any further blood bonds to other vampires and breaks existing ones.<br /> <br /> You can have infinite level 1 or 2 blood bonds so long as you don't have a level 3. If you have a level 3 bond, you can't have any other bonds. This is only one way though. You can have as many people with level 3 bonds to you as you can manage. You can just only have one level 3 bond to someone else.<br /> <br /> Bonds also wear off if you don't feed from the person again for roughly a year, so I guess you could just have a lot of level 1 bonds and just be careful not to feed from the same vampire more than once a year. Level 1 isn't so serious, and a lot of Elder vampires aren't terribly active and so don't need as much blood as younger vampires. Since the question seems directed at NPCs, a lot of Elders probably don't burn much more Vitae than one a day for waking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:33:40-08:00","id":1051099,"title":"","content":"Thank you all. <br /> Yes it was directed at NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:04:33-08:00","id":1051114,"title":"","content":"There is a Cruac rite that temporarily prevents Vinculum, and one of the Ordo's Mysteries centers around manipulating it. The Invictus have the Oath of Penance. Carthians have a law merit in the new supplement that can break a Vinc. A BP6+ vampire in any of these covenants would likely acquire the necessary abilities to circumvent blood bonds.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:11:04-08:00","id":1051120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051077#post1051077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can a Vampire be vinculated to only one vampire at time? I didn't know this...</div> </div> </div> </div>What Maina said. You can only be fully bound to one other person at a time but have as many as you can manage bonded to you.. <br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; Why should the sense of taste be the reason of a vinculum? Isn't it a mistical effect due to ingestion ov vampiric vitae? &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> The vinculum is established when one tastes vitae. If you have no sense of taste, you can't be affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:21:55-08:00","id":1051123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051120#post1051120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vinculum is established when one tastes vitae. If you have no sense of taste, you can't be affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing I didn't know. Thank' s a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T14:24:49-08:00","id":1051143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051123#post1051123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another thing I didn't know. Thank' s a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well becouse its not accurate. If you get vitae into your body, you get bloodbound. Even from a syringe with vitae or some spit in the eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:39:29-08:00","id":1051188,"title":"","content":"The different Covenants have different methods to deal with this. The ordo have specific Scales (fun fact Ordo can feed on a mortal they've infused with their own Vitae as if all the mortal's blood was Vitae.), Invictus have Fealty and Serfdom Oaths.<br /> <br /> Of course there are &quot;outside the box&quot; strategies like embracing a coma patient you're okay loving, protecting, and feeding mortal blood, a &quot;sleeping beauty&quot; blood-wife/husband so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-18-2017, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:05:51-08:00","id":1051290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051120#post1051120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vinculum is established when one tastes vitae. If you have no sense of taste, you can't be affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... &quot;taste Vitae&quot; probably meant &quot;eat, drink, or otherwise ingest Vitae&quot;, not &quot;fully be aware of the particular sensory stimulation held by Vitae.&quot; Natural language, and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:29:32-08:00","id":1051308,"title":"","content":"Surviving at high BP is a challenge and it's meant to be a challenge. It requires, at best, powerful sorceries to steal vitae or have it offered to you by willing supplicants, or at worst, get yourself blood bound to some neonate or another Elder.<br /> <br /> If you're not prepared for the long night, or unwilling to make sacrifices, then you've got to take a dirt nap for a few decades. This is why all Elders tend to be strong and dangerous. They had to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:10:07-08:00","id":1051413,"title":"","content":"There's always the option of using a reverent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T06:23:34-08:00","id":1051483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051290#post1051290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm... &quot;taste Vitae&quot; probably meant &quot;eat, drink, or otherwise ingest Vitae&quot;, not &quot;fully be aware of the particular sensory stimulation held by Vitae.&quot; Natural language, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you call &quot;natural language&quot; and say that's not the intent, I call unintended consequences of a power YOU didn't even consider yourself regarding application of the Touch of Deprivation power when or if you actually read it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T06:38:09-08:00","id":1051488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051483#post1051483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you call &quot;natural language&quot; and say that's not the intent, I call unintended consequences of a power YOU didn't even consider yourself regarding application of the Touch of Deprivation power when or if you actually read it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope -- Hermit's right. &quot;Taste&quot;, in this context, refers to ingestion. (It's a recurring holdover from the CWoD, across all editions of that as well as Requiem -- I/we have been down this road before, and it was addressed by The Powers That Be 2-3 forums ago.) It's conveying the idea that even a taste (as per a wine-sipping, or a lick) is sufficient to begin the Vinculum/Blood Oath/Blood Bond/&quot;I am going to own you&quot;. Whether the being in question can discern the flavor, texture or displaced aroma (as &quot;taste&quot; is as much and often more a conjoined function of scent/smelling as it is to do with the tongue) of the blood is completely irrelevant. (It's similar, cross-comparatively, to how a vinculum can be created via transfusion -- certainly no &quot;tasting&quot;, in any applied usage, is going on there, now is it...? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) Or would Touch of Deprivation, in your assessment, similarly prevent a vampire/whomever from being affected by an [appropriately ingested] poison, vis-a-vis laced blood or similar? (The answer to that, as well, is <i>no</i>.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T06:41:25-08:00","id":1051491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051483#post1051483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you call &quot;natural language&quot; and say that's not the intent, I call unintended consequences of a power YOU didn't even consider yourself regarding application of the Touch of Deprivation power when or if you actually read it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>And both are valid viewpoints to enjoy the game.<br /> <br /> Hmm... you now convinced me go to your side of the argument, and think of a vampire character who rips out his tongue to avoid tasting Vitae, and thus avoid blood bonds. Someone in the Ordo must have thought of this. Overly paranoid? Not enough when you're a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T06:51:43-08:00","id":1051495,"title":"","content":"By the way, the text states. : <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bond comes in three stages, usually at the first, second, and third <b><u>drinks</u></b>.<br /> <br /> Make a Blood Potency roll, minus the number of Vitae <b><u>ingested</u></b>. </div> </div> </div>I'm not native english and, in fact, my english really sucks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but it seems to me that the vitae need to be ingested, swallowed, not just tasted the flavor and spat out. But I could be wrong. Probably I can't find the &quot;taste&quot; reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T06:57:28-08:00","id":1051497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051495#post1051495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, the text states. :<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not native english and, in fact, my english really sucks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but it seems to me that the vitae need to be ingested, swallowed, not just tasted the flavor and spat out. But I could be wrong. Probably I can't find the &quot;taste&quot; reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part you quoted indeed makes it clear that it's not the sensory stimulus of taste that determines blood bonds. Not sure about other parts of the book, though. No need to be shy about non-native English <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:12:11-08:00","id":1051506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051491#post1051491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And both are valid viewpoints to enjoy the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid, contextually, to one's own house rules (which are always fine when everybody is having a good time); much less so, though, when addressing the RAW and the indicated intent across a number of editions of a game (as well as when keeping in mind the proper metaphysics of the setting in question)... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:51:22-08:00","id":1051519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051491#post1051491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And both are valid viewpoints to enjoy the game.<br /> <br /> Hmm... you now convinced me go to your side of the argument, and think of a vampire character who rips out his tongue to avoid tasting Vitae, and thus avoid blood bonds. Someone in the Ordo must have thought of this. Overly paranoid? Not enough when you're a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wanna play a character that does that every night to avoid vinculums, go for it. I'd certainly permit it. And wouldnt require you to play a Dragon to do it. It makes talking kind of difficult until you heal the damage. It's not like there aren't other cheaper or less time consuming powers with fewer risks than Touch of Deprivation that nullify vinculums or lets characters do things like rip their heart out and place it in a jar or ritualistically stake themselves to allow the vampire to ignore the torpor risk of getting a piece of wood shoved in their heart. Oh wait, there ARE cheap xp powers that lets a vampire character do precisely those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T11:19:07-08:00","id":1051588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051495#post1051495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, the text states. :<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not native english and, in fact, my english really sucks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but it seems to me that the vitae need to be ingested, swallowed, not just tasted the flavor and spat out. But I could be wrong. Probably I can't find the &quot;taste&quot; reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, Marcus. <br /> <br /> Also on page 99 Blood bonds<br /> <br /> While addictive, Vitae carries a far more sinister effect for<br /> those <b>who drink it:</b> the blood bond.<br /> <br /> <br /> To settle all this Taste vitae stuff the book says, ( first line page 100 &quot;blood bonds in play&quot;)<br /> <br /> Any time a character<b> imbibes a point or more of Vitae</b>, it<br /> creates or reinforces a blood bond. The bond comes in three<br /> stages, usually at the first, second, and third drinks<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Imbibe is drink or consume. Again. It has nothing to do with taste.</u> you can shoot up heroin and not taste it, but you still feel the effects of doing the drug..<br /> <br /> <br /> Later still if you keep reading<br /> <br /> Kindred characters can attempt to resist the bond by spending<br /> Willpower. Make a Blood Potency roll, minus the number of<br /> <b>Vitae ingested</b>. The Willpower point does not add to this roll.<br /> If successful,<b> that drink</b> does not add to the bond.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Page 59 for creating ghouls and we know that ghouls need to imbibe vitae in someway to become a ghoul, with all the draw backs of addiction and the bonding. Here are ways suggested in the book. ( pretty sure spitting in your eye, you dont taste it there... )<br /> <br /> A vampire need not press the prospective ghoul\u2019s lips to<br /> his wrist. There are so many other ways to skin that cat.<br /> <br /> The Serpent bites his lip, and you barely notice the copper<br /> in the kiss.<br /> <br /> The Haunt spits bloody phlegm in your eye, inexplicably, as<br /> you pass on the midnight road. Now you sit in your apartment<br /> feeling more afraid than you think you ought to, wondering<br /> if you should go get tested for some disease.<br /> <br /> You reach for your expensive coffee, but it tastes weird. A<br /> Shadow smiles in front of your face, but you cannot see her.<br /> You drank from a chalice when a Lord commanded you to.<br /> And now you\u2026no\u2026you don\u2019t quite remember what happened.<br /> <br /> The Savage cuts you and then herself, pressing the open<br /> wounds together. Something wild surges between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-19-2017, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:04:21-08:00","id":1051697,"title":"","content":"Yah, never heard this taste thing before, but it is pretty obvious that if you drink it, regardless of pinching your nose, it affects you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:30:35-08:00","id":1051716,"title":"","content":"Well I know that anyone can interpret the rules like he or she likes, but imho losing the sense of taste has nothing to do with vinculum. <b>If it was the case, every vampire would boil their tongue before drinking vitae to be vinculum proof</b>, since severe tongue wounds could cause losing the sense till it's healed. What is more, if losng the taste would be a protection. theban sorcorery vitae reliquary wouldn't casue vinculum and vitae addiction. Vinculum is something more mystical than just sensual.<br /> <br /> As it comes to feeding tactics at high BP. You can:<br /> 1. Go to torpor and loose enough BP<br /> 2. Feed from revenants, draugr. Create a revenant, keep him tied or staked in the basement, feed him human blood and drink the revenant's<br /> 3. Buy the feeding merit to feed from other supernatual beings (it's not easy, try to feed from a werewolf in kuruth)<br /> 4. Take the risk and feed from young vampires and try to resist the vinculum (feeding scenes must be great. Catch yourself a neonate or get blood bond)<br /> 5. Use Ordo Dracul scale to make human or animal blood suitable for you<br /> 6. Use Invictus oaths to get more vitae or not use vitae to rise each night<br /> 7. Maybe some blood magic as well<br /> 8. Get yourself blood bond with someone you trust (maybe perversion?) and forget about previous examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 02-19-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:11:43-08:00","id":1052681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1051716#post1051716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I know that anyone can interpret the rules like he or she likes, but imho losing the sense of taste has nothing to do with vinculum. <b>If it was the case, every vampire would boil their tongue before drinking vitae to be vinculum proof</b>, since severe tongue wounds could cause losing the sense till it's healed. What is more, if losng the taste would be a protection. theban sorcorery vitae reliquary wouldn't casue vinculum and vitae addiction. Vinculum is something more mystical than just sensual.<br /> <br /> As it comes to feeding tactics at high BP. You can:<br /> 1. Go to torpor and loose enough BP<br /> 2. Feed from revenants, draugr. Create a revenant, keep him tied or staked in the basement, feed him human blood and drink the revenant's<br /> 3. Buy the feeding merit to feed from other supernatual beings (it's not easy, try to feed from a werewolf in kuruth)<br /> 4. Take the risk and feed from young vampires and try to resist the vinculum (feeding scenes must be great. Catch yourself a neonate or get blood bond)<br /> 5. Use Ordo Dracul scale to make human or animal blood suitable for you<br /> 6. Use Invictus oaths to get more vitae or not use vitae to rise each night<br /> 7. Maybe some blood magic as well<br /> 8. Get yourself blood bond with someone you trust (maybe perversion?) and forget about previous examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, perversion makes a hell of a lot more sense than a lot of Invictus dynasties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T06:48:54-08:00","id":1053166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1052681#post1052681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, perversion makes a hell of a lot more sense than a lot of Invictus dynasties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that feeding problems aren't the only reason to create a dynasty. Of course they can pass the office when someone is in torpor, but it's also about prestige, trust and solid authority over a domain. In many cases it's more difficult to remove 3 figures than only one prince. I agree that in some situations perversion is easier to maintain than a dynasty. However, perversion and dynasty don't exclude themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:15:17-08:00","id":1053178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1052681#post1052681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, perversion makes a hell of a lot more sense than a lot of Invictus dynasties.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have two vampires over 6BP and in both cases I found that the perversion was easiest, but then for my BP 10 vampire I have taken unnatural affinity for werewolves and changelings as it was hard for the vampire to maintain full vitae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:25:08-08:00","id":1053186,"title":"","content":"I thought Maxwell handled it pretty well. He risked addiction on another vampire, but chose a 'hearty' vampire with no political ambition. Maybe in a few decades he'd change his mind, but by then maybe Maxwell could find a replacement.<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood had a potential other option, as they were able to practice vaulderie, which bonded one to their covey, rather than an individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-22-2017, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:09:44-08:00","id":1053219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053178#post1053178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have two vampires over 6BP and in both cases I found that the perversion was easiest, but then for my BP 10 vampire I have taken unnatural affinity for werewolves and changelings as it was hard for the vampire to maintain full vitae</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, BP8+ vampires have less antagonists to fear, so even feeding from a werewolf isn't a big thing. For younger Kindred it's still a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053186#post1053186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Belial's Brood had a potential other option, as they were able to practice vaulderie, which bonded one to their covey, rather than an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Sabbat did in Masqurade.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:27:33-08:00","id":1053225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053219#post1053219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, BP8+ vampires have less antagonists to fear, so even feeding from a werewolf isn't a big thing. For younger Kindred it's still a problem.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Serial Diablerie gets you up there fast! However my last Antagonist was a demon who had a bunch of fire attacks. It was pretty nasty as he had a lot of lackies too. I would say the best way to take out a higher BP vampire ( or at least give them a nasty challenge ) is to overwhelm them with supernatural baddies.<br /> <br /> About the werewolf thing though, It depends on your ST if you can befriend a wolf, it might make things easier. So you wouldn't have to hunt them down and feed violently, but you could call in a favor or pay them or something..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:14:41-08:00","id":1053256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053178#post1053178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have two vampires over 6BP and in both cases I found that the perversion was easiest, but then for my BP 10 vampire I have taken unnatural affinity for werewolves and changelings as it was hard for the vampire to maintain full vitae</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The difficulty in this is that it assumes Werewolves and Changelings even exist in your world. If you're just doing Blue Book + Vampire, then the only things unnatural affinity work for are ghosts, spirits, maybe the God Machine Angels, and Strix.<br /> <br /> And feeding from ephemeral beings can sometimes be more difficult than perversion, or sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:27:40-08:00","id":1053266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053225#post1053225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the werewolf thing though, It depends on your ST if you can befriend a wolf, it might make things easier. So you wouldn't have to hunt them down and feed violently, but you could call in a favor or pay them or something..</div> </div> </div> </div>An excellent example of this would be the Dead Wolves bloodline from <i>Shadows of Mexico</i> that are members of werewolf packs. Imagine local Hispanic vampires who have a heart for their community backed by the werewolf pack they are directly related to, Diablerizing all the Gringo vampires attempting to invade their little slice of the world taking Unnatural Affinity so they can be the old members of a multi-generational pack dating back to the Aztecs. The spirit and werewolf savvy/loyal Elders that could produce would be stifling to younger vampires, prompting younger vampire migration from that area.<br /> <br /> Not that the Dead Wolves have a monopoly on that tactic, it seems rather common for the Mexican vampires to have alliances with werewolves. And given the broader definition of 'Pack' in Second edition werewolf, it is likely that there would be packs with vampires of many different bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-22-2017, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:54:32-08:00","id":1053320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053256#post1053256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The difficulty in this is that it assumes Werewolves and Changelings even exist in your world. If you're just doing Blue Book + Vampire, then the only things unnatural affinity work for are ghosts, spirits, maybe the God Machine Angels, and Strix.<br /> <br /> And feeding from ephemeral beings can sometimes be more difficult than perversion, or sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why it would entirely depend on what you and your story teller are going through. <br /> <br /> I have been playing the game with my serial diablerist for 2+ years almost on a daily basis and the other one I played for 3 years but it came to an end we needed variety to keep the game flowing. Anyway, there was everything. Assuming CofD+Vampire are the only things in my world is a terrible assumption. I know that &quot;my world&quot; and &quot;your world&quot; are very very different worlds which is absolutely ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:10:51-08:00","id":1053332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053320#post1053320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's why it would entirely depend on what you and your story teller are going through.<br /> <br /> I have been playing the game with my serial diablerist for 2+ years almost on a daily basis and the other one I played for 3 years but it came to an end we needed variety to keep the game flowing. Anyway, there was everything. Assuming CofD+Vampire are the only things in my world is a terrible assumption. I know that &quot;my world&quot; and &quot;your world&quot; are very very different worlds which is absolutely ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, I meant no offense if you took any from what I said. Any ST is free to present their world as they do. I've just always played Requiem as just Core+Vampire and have always assumed that is the 'default' to Vampire unless the ST decides to incorporate other venues. Indeed, if there are other supernaturals and you have access to them, then feeding at higher BP with affinity is easier than if you can only feed from other Kindred and the ephemeral. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:55:45-08:00","id":1053479,"title":"","content":"In our Vampire Requiem games the world isn't too supernatural heavy or at least the supernatural beings don't know too much about each other. In many cases some of them can live next to each other and coexist, but I get it that keeping the game same for years is boring, so it's good to change the campaign type. Back in Vampire Dark Ages we used to play more supernatural. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053225#post1053225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Serial Diablerie gets you up there fast! However my last Antagonist was a demon who had a bunch of fire attacks. It was pretty nasty as he had a lot of lackies too. I would say the best way to take out a higher BP vampire ( or at least give them a nasty challenge ) is to overwhelm them with supernatural baddies.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's your Serial Diablerie strategy to be unpunished? Is it Plausible Deniability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:21:18-08:00","id":1053555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053479#post1053479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your Serial Diablerie strategy to be unpunished? Is it Plausible Deniability?</div> </div> </div> </div>Long story.... to sum it up briefly at the cost of it possibly not sounding interesting:<br /> <br /> He was turned and always tried to do the right thing but people around him started dying. He was dating his sire who becamep prince because the old prince and sheriff when up in flames ( from a human fire starter / other player ) my character was appointed new sheriff. He sure didn't want the job and all &quot;his people&quot; kept getting attacked, so he thought if he could get stronger faster people would stop attacking the city and his lover. He started diablerizing all the baddies. Somewhere in there he became bound to the prince and the prince to him(perversion), but then they tried to stop him and break the addiction and it went well for a while .... <br /> <br /> He quit being the sheriff and was appointed voice. But then some other baddies rolled into town and he ate them all. It was pretty fucked up really. It's like the sleeping tiger, everyone is pretty much afraid to call him on it, and he tries really hard only to eat the bad ones trying to kill People. <br /> <br /> However now he is kind of &quot;retired&quot; and his lover has passed the prince position off too.<br /> <br /> Ok, longer than expected but he is like the boogeyman now, sanctioned and used by the prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-22-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T19:00:49-08:00","id":1053572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1051059-feeding-at-high-bp?p=1053555#post1053555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Long story.... to sum it up briefly at the cost of it possibly not sounding interesting:<br /> <br /> He was turned and always tried to do the right thing but people around him started dying. He was dating his sire who becamep prince because the old prince and sheriff when up in flames ( from a human fire starter / other player ) my character was appointed new sheriff. He sure didn't want the job and all &quot;his people&quot; kept getting attacked, so he thought if he could get stronger faster people would stop attacking the city and his lover. He started diablerizing all the baddies. Somewhere in there he became bound to the prince and the prince to him(perversion), but then they tried to stop him and break the addiction and it went well for a while ....<br /> <br /> He quit being the sheriff and was appointed voice. But then some other baddies rolled into town and he ate them all. It was pretty fucked up really. It's like the sleeping tiger, everyone is pretty much afraid to call him on it, and he tries really hard only to eat the bad ones trying to kill People.<br /> <br /> However now he is kind of &quot;retired&quot; and his lover has passed the prince position off too.<br /> <br /> Ok, longer than expected but he is like the boogeyman now, sanctioned and used by the prince.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh I see, almost like Crypteia in Lords over Damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}